{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the codebase technical-debt review at exact head 650f0c535b0b86e8499439776e44590ebcd4d51f, tree 444a358045e8050d6ad14b6ed376b39327eab3d8, on planner/techdebt-review-20261025 (review request c50383a9, my promise 224b5b71). This review binds request 72a6df7d (promise 482d8baf) to this one candidate. The head is document-only: one new note, notes/2026-10-25-codebase-techdebt-review.md, 699 lines. No gate is needed and none ran; source and tests are unchanged, and the merge into Main 1f3feea2 gives the head's own tree 444a3580. It may land. The answer to the section 6 question is below; the builder requests follow after landing, in the section 8 order, as the request says.\n\nRead order: the note first and in full, then the request and its conditions, then every cited file at Main c8a3fb24, the planner's evidence folder, and the replay and delivery code behind section 6. The worktree /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-worktrees/planner-techdebt-20261024 is clean at the head on its branch; the merge-base is 1f3feea2, one commit above; git diff --check is clean; check-commit-messages reports 1 checked, 0 flagged; the one artifact event names the one changed path; the note has no Markdown links; the section-citation check on an export of the head exits 0 with the four known unresolved references, unchanged.\n\nConditions of c50383a9 and 72a6df7d, each checked:\n1. Documents only: yes, one note.\n2. Evidence and method. The note gives 211 path citations. I checked every full-path citation against c8a3fb24 by script, and the 23 short-form ones (a bare file name after the full path) by hand; every cited line says what the note says it says, and every cited range lies inside its file. The three paths the note names as absent or historical (notes/README.md, the proposed wrangler.artroom-scope.jsonc, the old page-assets.ts path) are stated as such. The evidence folder /private/tmp/artroom-planner-techdebt-20261025 verifies: SHA256SUMS lists 85 files,